course: dictionary
lesson: 12533
title: Destroyed and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Destroy means to damage something so badly that it no longer exists or cannot be used. «The storm destroyed the old barn.» After the storm the barn is gone, so destroyed tells you what happened to it.
explain: Destroyed is the past form of destroy, so it tells us the damage has already happened. It can also describe a thing. «The destroyed bridge was closed for a year.» Here destroyed means completely ruined. Check it by swapping in «completely ruined»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Destroyed can also have informal meanings. «After the long match, the team felt destroyed.» The match and the word felt tell you the players were very tired or very upset. Always read the words around the word to find its meaning.
fact: Destroy means to damage something so badly that it no longer exists or cannot be used.
fact: The forms are destroy, destroys, destroying and destroyed.
fact: «Destroyed» as an adjective means completely ruined.
fact: «Destroyed» can also mean very upset or very tired, and in a game it can mean beaten very badly.
fact: Fires, floods, earthquakes and wars can destroy buildings, and people then work out how to rebuild them.
exercise: «The fire destroyed the wooden school.» What does destroyed mean here? | Made bigger and stronger | Painted and repaired | *Damaged so badly it no longer exists
exercise: Which word is the past form of destroy? | destroys | *destroyed | destroying
exercise: After a long match, Sam says, «I feel totally destroyed.» What does he probably mean? | He has won a prize | He is painting a picture | He has found a lost dog | *He is very tired
test: «The earthquake destroyed many old homes in the village.» What does destroyed mean? | Made them warmer | *Ruined so badly they could not be used | Painted bright colours | Moved them to the hill
test: Which sentence uses destroyed to describe a thing? | *The destroyed tent lay in the mud. | The storm destroyed the tent. | She destroyed her old toy.
exam: Why might people rebuild a town after it is destroyed? | Because the town is too tall | *Because the buildings were ruined and people still need homes | Because the town has been forgotten | Because the town was painted
